#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:5
#: c8f8821a0a7642c18ca65bad2bcbba0e
msgid "Inverted Flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:7
#: 789b7cbd10d14210bb7ca38f6c907c40
msgid "Plane supports inverted flight. Inverted flight is initiated by setting an RC channel via RCx_OPTION parameter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:10
#: 8c8346ad1cf946448fb8ff0083366a2c
msgid "Details"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:12
#: b8cface07b294cf39004a21e207c1675
msgid "The RCx_OPTION parameter allows you to configure a transmitter switch to enable inverted flight for fixed wing aircraft. To enable it, choose a RC input channel which is not being used for anything else, and setup your transmitter to give a PWM value larger than 1750 when a previously unused 2 position switch is enabled, and a value below 1200 when it is not enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:19
#: 7fe751efc1e941e8aceb37ed932efe74
msgid "For example, if channel 7 is currently unused, and you set :ref:`RC7_OPTION<RC7_OPTION>` to InvertedFlight (which has value 43) then if your transmitter sends 1900 on channel 7 the plane will flip upside down and continue flying in whatever mode it is in, but with the plane inverted."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:25
#: 8e37e7d94dd046f5bff146f302937017
msgid "Transmitter Setup"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:27
#: fcb8a96208214f1dadecf0b4e29a6aa8
msgid "Enabling inverted flight only changes how ArduPilot stabilises the plane. It will stabilise it with a roll of 180 degrees from normal whenever inverted flight is enabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:31
#: 0270fac0858f424aae85a75b1215f54b
msgid "To get the most out of inverted flight it can be useful to also invert your transmitter elevator and rudder controls while your inverted flight switch is enabled. This should be possible with any good transmitter."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:36
#: 7aaeb200b4164ab48686b48f8d1aa188
msgid "Interaction with flight modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:38
#: 5af71aa18e91487cacf780ce038128d3
msgid "Inverted flight can be used with any of the non-quadplane stabilized flight modes (which means anything but manual mode). That means you can switch on inverted flight during a mission and the plane will continue the mission inverted. Make sure you disable it before trying to land!"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:45
#: 30f56e81a8694ee5b19157d633451ab2
msgid "Tips"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:47
#: d44a73f3124f4c0a8149068aec01a132
msgid "Here are some general tips about inverted flight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:49
#: 0f13a940ff484a7aa49d86f809f4de9a
msgid "Try it out in simulation first to get used to it, and ensure your transmitter is setup right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:51
#: a7040e062e494757acb03e7a254d594a
msgid "make sure you have plenty of height before engaging or disengaging inverted flight. Depending on your airframe, you could lose a lot of height while flipping over, and it may be that your airframe struggles to maintain height while inverted"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/inverted-flight.rst:55
#: ae430ef9f2664c87999ab1f530ebc5c6
msgid "make sure your ``PTCH2SRV_I`` value and ``PTCH2SRV_IMAX`` is high enough. Planes commonly need more pitch trim while inverted to hold height."
msgstr ""
